{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793686612317651076,"compiled_state":{"alias":"asthmatic-grave-caudata","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":2},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793681149248235001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"29061aaf-dbe9-4d1c-b219-178c753a9707","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1712-f158-9314-420a"}],"description":"## Observation\nA `cp -R` (or `cp -r`) copy of a linked git worktree is not an isolated copy. It keeps the original's `.git` file (`gitdir: <common>/.git/worktrees/<name>`), so any git command run in the copy resolves to the original repository. `git -C <copy> rev-parse --git-common-dir` returns the shared `.git`.\n\nReproduced 2026-11-02 in a sandbox: fresh repo with `origin` and `gerrit` remotes, `git worktree add ../wt`, `cp -R ../wt ../wt-copy`, then `git -C ../wt-copy remote remove <r>` for each remote. Afterwards `git remote -v` in the main checkout was empty.\n\nOn this host the same construction (a \"throwaway\" `tracker-copy` of `.tickets-tracker` under `.rebar/scratch/`) did two things on 2026-10-27. It removed both remotes from the shared `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.git/config` (bug `affordable-omphacite-sunfish`). It also landed REBUILD SNAPSHOT commits on the real local `tickets` branch (bug `painted-epidermal-shelduck`).\n\n## Impact\nAny recipe that does \"work on a copy of the tracker\" with a file copy can rewrite shared config, move shared refs, and take shared locks. Nothing warns about this, and the damage shows up later as unrelated-looking failures.\n\n## Open question for the plan\nHow to guard it: rebar could refuse to operate on (or warn about) a worktree whose path does not match the `gitdir` back-pointer recorded in `<common>/worktrees/<name>/gitdir`. Alternatively, a sanctioned \"isolated tracker copy\" helper could use `git clone`/`git worktree add` and be documented in `docs/concurrency.md`. Not decided.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A rebar command run inside a file-copied linked worktree of the tracker either refuses with a message naming the copy hazard or operates only on an isolated repository, verified by a test that copies a linked worktree and asserts the shared `.git/config` and branch refs are unchanged.\n- [ ] `docs/concurrency.md` documents the hazard and the sanctioned way to make an isolated tracker copy.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"fb16-a8b0-c2b7-449a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"A cp -R copy of a linked worktree is a live handle on the shared repo: git commands in the copy rewrite shared config and refs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["60586cf0-e4bf-46fb-93d5-9a59bf35fd55","29061aaf-dbe9-4d1c-b219-178c753a9707"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793686612317651076,"uuid":"de310bf3-4302-426e-b83c-a3f503b3bda4"}